    "science": "Key Active Ingredients: \nHyaluronic Acid \nMOA: Topical hyaluronic acid (HA) acts primarily as a high-capacity humectant, binding up to 1,000 times its weight in water to the skin surface to provide immediate hydration, plumping, and smoothing effects. It works by forming a breathable, moisture-retaining film, decreasing transepidermal water loss (TEWL) while reducing fine lines and enhancing skin elasticity.\n•\tEnhances hydration \n•\tSupports collagen function and skin structure\nTopical hyaluronic acid (HA) is scientifically proven to significantly increase skin hydration (up to 134% immediately, ~55% at 6 weeks) and improve elasticity. \nRef :\nhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10078143/\nhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8322246/#:~:text=The%20HA%20serum%20demonstrated%20excellent,an%20excellent%20skin%20tolerability%20profile.\n\nAllantoin \nAllantoin functions as a multi-stage cell-regenerating agent. It speeds up the skin's transition from an inflammatory state to a proliferative phase, making it a staple for wound healing, scar reduction, and severe barrier repair\nHas anti-inflammatory and antioxidant effects. It has been shown to repair cutaneous photodamage and reduce inflammation following UVR exposure. \nMOA: It operates by strictly regulating the localized inflammatory response, directly stimulating fibroblastic proliferation, and accelerating the synthesis of the extracellular matrix (dermal scaffolding)\nRef:\nhttps://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20877959/\nhttps://www.jaad.org/article/S0190-9622(17)30663-1/abstract\nhttps://www.researchgate.net/publication/46580052_Profile_of_wound_healing_process_induced_by_allantoin\nhttps://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/medicine-and-dentistry/allantoin\n \n\n\nSalvia Officinalis (Sage) Extract\nHas natural deodorizing effect due to its antibacterial properties  \nAnti-Inflammatory and Antioxidant Properties\nSage extracts downregulate the expression of key pro-inflammatory cytokines, specifically Interleukin-6 (IL-6), Interleukin-1β (IL-1β), and Tumor Necrosis Factor-alpha (TNF-α). Ursolic acid within the plant interferes with the NF-κB transcription factor, stopping the signals that trigger localized cellular swelling and pain\nSage (Salvia officinalis) extract enriched for ursolic acid clinically reduces skin sensitivity to irritants and lightens the appearance of facial hyperpigmentary spots\nRef:\nhttps://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24497852/\nhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7922507/#sec4-antioxidants-10-00311\nhttps://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17713873/\nhttps://www.researchgate.net/publication/313139838_Topical_application_of_Salvia_officinalis_hydroethanolic_leaf_extract_improves_wound_healing_process\nhttps://www.jaad.org/article/S0190-9622(18)31799-7/abstract"
