    "science": "Key Active Ingredients: \nUV Filter System\nPhotostable, Broad-spectrum UVA/UVB filters\nUV Filter (INCI) | UV Coverage\nEthylhexyl Methoxycinnamate | UVB\nMethylene Bis-Benzotriazolyl Tetramethylbutylphenol (nano) | Broad-spectrum UVA + UVB\nButyl Methoxydibenzoylmethane | UVA\nEthylhexyl Salicylate | UVB\nBenzophenone-3 | UVA + UVB\n\nRef:\nhttps://www.mdpi.com/2079-9284/10/4/101\nhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8361399/\n\n\nSalvia Officinalis (Sage) Extract\n\nAnti-Inflammatory and Antioxidant Properties\nSage extracts downregulate the expression of key pro-inflammatory cytokines, specifically Interleukin-6 (IL-6), Interleukin-1β (IL-1β), and Tumor Necrosis Factor-alpha (TNF-α). Ursolic acid within the plant interferes with the NF-κB transcription factor, stopping the signals that trigger localized cellular swelling and pain\nimproves wound healing process\nSage triggers a multi-step cellular repair sequence. It upregulates the genetic expression of Fibroblast Growth Factor-2 (FGF-2) and Vascular Endothelial Growth Factor (VEGF). This forces rapid cellular multiplication, stimulates angiogenesis (new blood vessel growth), and increases hydroxyproline—the primary structural building block of skin collagen\nSage (Salvia officinalis) extract enriched for ursolic acid clinically reduces skin sensitivity to irritants and lightens the appearance of facial hyperpigmentary spots\nRef:\nhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7922507/#sec4-antioxidants-10-00311\nhttps://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17713873/\nhttps://www.researchgate.net/publication/313139838_Topical_application_of_Salvia_officinalis_hydroethanolic_leaf_extract_improves_wound_healing_process\nhttps://www.jaad.org/article/S0190-9622(18)31799-7/abstract\n\nWitch Hazel Extract (Hamamelis Virginiana)\n\nPossess strong antioxidant and anti-inflammatory properties.\nantibacterial, \nantifungal, \nantiviral, \nwound healing properties: Hamamelis also promotes wound healing by modulating enzymes, reducing oxidative damage, and stimulating skin cell growth\nClinical studies support its use in eczema, acne, UV-induced erythema, and sensitive scalp conditions\nwith improved skin barrier function\n\nRef:\nhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12250947/#sec5-molecules-30-02744\nhttps://www.jaad.org/article/S0190-9622(24)02437-X/fulltext\nhttps://www.researchgate.net/publication/386047423_Revealing_the_Therapeutic_Potential_Investigating_the_Impact_of_a_Novel_Witch_Hazel_Formula_on_Anti-Inflammation_and_Antioxidation\n\n\nUrea\nUrea plays a fundamental role in regulating keratinocyte proliferation, the skin's barrier function and antimicrobial defense and maintain healthy skin\n\nRef:\nhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8611129/"
